---
// One event of a simulation run, step by step: generators → stack → engine → steps → sensitive volume →
// MC points → secondaries → end of the event → output tree. The engine in this walk-through is TGeant3, the
// default engine of examples/simulation/Tutorial1/macros/run_tutorial1.C (line 24), with the example stack
// (examples/common/mcstack/FairStack) and the detector FairTutorialDet1 of that example.
// Differences from Tutorial1: the macro adds one FairBoxGenerator only (run_tutorial1.C:105-113); the diagram
// adds a FairParticleGenerator to show two generators. The geometry (examples/common/geometry/double_sector.geo)
// has two sensitive volumes, tutdet1 and tutdet2; the diagram shows tutdet1 only. With the default geometry
// model "TGeo" (fairroot/base/steer/FairRunSim.h:263), g3Config.C makes a TGeant3TGeo
// (examples/common/gconfig/g3Config.C:17-18). TGeant3TGeo derives from TGeant3 and uses its event loop
// (vmc-project/geant3 TGeant3/TGeant3TGeo.cxx: GtreveRoot() calls the same gtreveroot), so the diagram uses the
// engine name TGeant3, as in run->SetName("TGeant3").
//
// Facts (FairRoot, paths relative to the repository):
// - FairRunSim::Run() calls fApp->RunMC(NEvents) (fairroot/base/steer/FairRunSim.cxx:322-324).
//   FairMCApplication::RunMC() calls fMC->ProcessRun(nofEvents) (fairroot/base/sim/FairMCApplication.cxx:302).
// - FairMCApplication::BeginEvent() calls BeginEvent() of each active detector (FairMCApplication.cxx:384-390).
// - FairMCApplication::GeneratePrimaries() calls fEvGen->GenerateEvent(fStack) (FairMCApplication.cxx:982-990).
//   FairPrimaryGenerator::GenerateEvent() calls MakeVertex(), then ReadEvent(this) of each generator in fGenList
//   (fairroot/base/sim/FairPrimaryGenerator.cxx:224-281, MakeVertex 245, ReadEvent 262).
//   FairBoxGenerator::ReadEvent() and FairParticleGenerator::ReadEvent() call primGen->AddTrack()
//   (fairroot/generators/FairBoxGenerator.cxx:219, FairParticleGenerator.cxx:64). AddTrack() adds the event
//   vertex to the track vertex (FairPrimaryGenerator.cxx:302-304) and calls fStack->PushTrack() with parent -1
//   (FairPrimaryGenerator.cxx:371, 382).
// - FairStack: fStack is a std::stack<TParticle*>, last in, first out (examples/common/mcstack/FairStack.h:218).
//   PushTrack() pushes the particle onto fStack if toBeDone == 1 (FairStack.cxx:83-131, push 130).
//   PopNextTrack() takes fStack.top() and pops it; on an empty stack it sets iTrack = -1 and returns nullptr
//   (FairStack.cxx:134-156). AddPoint(detId) counts a point for the current track in fPointsMap (336-347).
//   FillTrackArray() copies the selected particles into the MCTrack array, with their point counts (196-238,
//   SetNPoints 225); SelectTracks() always keeps the primaries (383-458). UpdateTrackIndex() puts the new track
//   numbers into the MC points of each detector collection (245-300). Reset() clears fStack, the particles, the
//   tracks and the point counts (302-313). Register(): branch "MCTrack" (318).
// - FairMCApplication::Stepping(): id = fMC->CurrentVolID(copyNo), fVolMap.find(id), the FairVolume with the same
//   copy number, disvol->GetDetector(), disdet->ProcessHits(disvol) (FairMCApplication.cxx:514-528). fVolMap
//   (std::multimap<Int_t, FairVolume*>, FairMCApplication.h:295) holds only the sensitive volumes: InitGeometry()
//   fills it from FairModule::fAllSensitiveVolumes (FairMCApplication.cxx:882-918). RegisterSensitiveVolume()
//   calls vol.SetModule(this), and FairVolume::SetModule() sets fDetector (fairroot/base/sim/FairModule.cxx:217-223,
//   FairVolume.cxx:31-35).
// - FairTutorialDet1 (examples/simulation/Tutorial1/src/FairTutorialDet1.cxx): IsSensitive() is true for volume
//   names with "tutdet" (118-121). ProcessHits() adds Edep() of each step (68); when the track exits, stops or
//   disappears, it calls AddHit() and stack->AddPoint(kTutDet) (71-88); with no energy loss it makes no point
//   (75-77), so the diagram assumes that each track loses energy in tutdet1. EndOfEvent() clears the points (94).
//   Register(): branch "TutorialDetPoint" (104).
// - FairMCApplication::FinishEvent() order (FairMCApplication.cxx:633-671): fStack->FillTrackArray() (646),
//   fStack->UpdateTrackIndex() (648), the task list if there is one (652-655, not shown), FinishEvent() of each
//   active detector (658), fRootManager->Fill() (662), EndOfEvent() of each active detector (668),
//   fStack->Reset() (671). fairroot/base/sim/FairDetector.h:56 and 101 say the same: EndOfEvent() after and
//   FinishEvent() before the tree fill.
// - FairRootManager::Fill() calls fSink->Fill() (fairroot/base/steer/FairRootManager.cxx:331-334).
//   FairRootFileSink::Fill() calls fOutTree->Fill() (fairroot/base/sink/FairRootFileSink.cxx:302-305). The
//   default tree name is "cbmsim" (FairRootManager.cxx:943). FairMCEventHeader registers "MCEventHeader."
//   (fairroot/base/event/FairMCEventHeader.cxx:85). The sink writes the tree to the file at the end of the run:
//   FinishRun() → fRootManager->Write() (FairMCApplication.cxx:369) → fSink->Write() (FairRootManager.cxx:353)
//   → WriteTObject(fOutTree) (FairRootFileSink.cxx:328).
// Facts (VMC engines, github.com/vmc-project/geant3 and geant4_vmc):
// - TGeant3::ProcessRun() calls ProcessEvent() for each event: BeginEvent(), Gtrig(), FinishEvent()
//   (TGeant3/TGeant3.cxx). Gtrig calls gukine → GeneratePrimaries() (TGeant3gu.cxx) and gtreve_root, which pops
//   tracks with stack->PopNextTrack() (rxgtrak) until there are none and calls BeginPrimary() for each primary
//   (gtrak/gtreveroot.F). gutrak: PreTrack(), the tracking, PostTrack(). gustep: the secondaries of the step
//   go to SetTrack(1, current track, ...) → PushTrack(), then Stepping().
// - TGeant4 is different: it reads the primaries with PopPrimaryForTracking() and tracks from its own stack
//   (TG4PrimaryGeneratorAction.cxx, TG4TrackManager.cxx).
// Not shown: FinishPrimary(), the task list, the track selection cuts of FairStack.
import Explainer from './Explainer.astro';

const steps = [
  {
    cap: 'FairRunSim::Run() starts the transport engine, here TGeant3. At the start of each event, the engine calls BeginEvent(), and FairMCApplication calls BeginEvent() of each active detector.',
    code: 'fMC->ProcessRun(nofEvents);',
  },
  {
    cap: 'The engine calls GeneratePrimaries(). FairPrimaryGenerator makes the event vertex, then each generator reads its particles and puts them onto the stack with AddTrack().',
    code: 'primGen->AddTrack(GetPDGType(), px, py, pz, fX, fY, fZ);',
  },
  {
    cap: 'TGeant3 takes the track on top of the stack with PopNextTrack(): last in, first out. (TGeant4 reads the primaries with PopPrimaryForTracking() and uses its own stack.)',
    code: 'std::stack<TParticle*> fStack;',
  },
  {
    cap: 'The engine moves the track in steps and calls Stepping() after each step. In a sensitive volume, Stepping() finds the FairVolume from the volume ID and the copy number, and calls ProcessHits() of its detector.',
    code: 'disdet->ProcessHits(disvol);',
  },
  {
    cap: 'A step in the volume makes a secondary track. TGeant3 pushes it onto the stack, with the current track as its mother.',
    code: 'fStack.push(particle);',
  },
  {
    cap: 'The track leaves the volume. ProcessHits() of the detector adds a point with the energy loss in the volume, and AddPoint() counts the point for the track.',
    code: 'stack->AddPoint(kTutDet);',
  },
  {
    cap: 'The engine transports the other tracks in the same way: first the secondary, then #0. When the stack is empty, PopNextTrack() returns no track.',
    code: 'if (fStack.empty()) { iTrack = -1; return nullptr; }',
  },
  {
    cap: 'The engine calls FinishEvent(). FillTrackArray() copies the tracks into the MCTrack array, and UpdateTrackIndex() puts the new track numbers into the points.',
    code: 'fStack->FillTrackArray();',
  },
  {
    cap: 'FairRootManager::Fill() makes the sink add one entry to the tree cbmsim (the sink writes the tree to the file at the end of the run). Then EndOfEvent() clears the points, and Reset() clears the stack.',
    code: 'fRootManager->Fill();',
  },
];

// Beats inside each step: [time in ms, texts]. At beat i (i ≥ 1) the script adds the class b<i> to the stage.
// It writes the texts into the elements with data-k: a0…a4 call trace of FairMCApplication, eng TGeant3,
// st FairStack, det FairTutorialDet1, nS tracks on the stack, nP points, ent entries of the tree. A step starts
// from empty texts, except the counters nS, nP and ent, which each step sets at time 0.
type Beat = [number, Record<string, string>];
const at0 = (nS: number, nP: number) => ({ nS: String(nS), nP: String(nP), ent: 'cbmsim: 0 entries' });
const beats: Beat[][] = [
  [
    [0, { ...at0(0, 0), eng: 'ProcessRun()', a0: 'BeginEvent()' }],
    [500, { a1: '→ BeginEvent()', det: 'BeginEvent()' }],
  ],
